{"seq":24,"trial_id":"gbrain-memory-2026-10/openclaw-haiku-gbrain-told-live-mu-memory/ms-05-vantorre-tickets/r1","wall_ts":"2026-10-27T02:17:44.355Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-16T09:00:00-05:00","args_digest":"218adead2cff45a7aa68036b468ec5a38c3343d121578a9a35ab75984c15bbea","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"C36LMHRLAXI","text":"Hi Nadia, here's what I found for Vantorre Group (the parent, not Mobility). I checked #strategic-pod, #inc-vtg-hartford and the Moss Strategic digests in the shared files. I don't have access to the ticketing system, so this is only what appears in those sources.\n\n**Tickets found**\n\n1. **#8841**, #strategic-pod, 2026-07-01 (Gideon Sato): closed with support after IT cleared a browser cache issue on the kiosk tablets.\n2. **#8841**, Moss digest 2026-05-04: still open, a gate kiosk timeout at Allentown, Dock Door 12, second shift.\n3. **#PD-8841**, Moss digest 2026-04-27: two missed carrier check-ins at Allentown, Gate 4, second shift.\n4. **#8841**, Moss digest 2026-09-30: Mateo's report that Newark drivers can't select Dock Door 14 on the check-in kiosk, escalated to platform engineering.\n5. **INC-4821**, #inc-vtg-hartford, 2026-08-03 (Gideon): Mateo's status-page access problem. The screenshot is attached there and Gideon was still chasing it.\n6. **VT-55120**, #inc-vtg-hartford, 2026-10-14 (Gideon): the root-cause ticket for the Hartford kiosk outage, with Carrowmere's gateway route finding and reconnect log attached.\n\n**Things to check before the steering committee**\n\n- **#8841 is used for three different issues.** The pod channel says it was closed on 7/1, the 5/4 digest says it was open at Allentown Door 12, and the 9/30 digest says it's a Newark Door 14 issue. It may have been reused or refiled. I can't tell from these sources which is right, so someone should confirm in the ticketing system.\n- The Moss digest from 2026-08-03 covers the Hartford incident but gives no ticket number.\n- The Moss digest from 2025-09-15 lists #PD-4418 (Carrier_Dwell_Summary export, Dock Door 9) under \"the account Nadia runs\" without naming the account, so I've left it out. Tell me if it belongs to Vantorre Group and I'll add it.\n- I left out #4812 (Vantorre Mobility) and #PD-4402 (Quillfeather), since they aren't parent tickets."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"C36LMHRLAXI","ts":"1792159200.000126"}}
